# Provenance

`openmoc3` is a Rust reader for Live2D `.moc3` model files.

## What it derives from

**Sakura Motion / PurismCore** <https://github.com/SakuraMotion/PurismCore>
MIT licensed. A C99 reimplementation of Cubism Core with v6 support. Portions
of this crate's structure and its version-dependent constants derive from that
work. Their copyright notice is preserved in LICENSE, as MIT requires.

**OpenL2D Project** <https://github.com/OpenL2D/moc3ingbird>
Free Development Public License 1.0-US. `src/moc3.hexpat` names every field in
moc3 v3.00 through v5.00. Its README states: "you are free to use the included
model files and pattern files to create your own MOC3 readers and writers. No
license will restrict your right to do so." The malformed `exploit.moc3` from
that repository (CVE-2023-27566) is used as a fuzz seed.

**Live2D Inc.'s published documentation**
The JSON sidecar specifications at <https://github.com/Live2D/CubismSpecs> and
the Standard Parameter List in the Cubism Editor manual. Public documentation,
used as published.

**Our own analysis**
Section extents, element widths and field semantics verified independently
across five models spanning three format versions, by decoding every section
into typed values and re-encoding it byte-identically. Method and results are
in `ayatsuri2d-research/docs/`.

## What it does NOT derive from

No Live2D software was installed. No Live2D binary was disassembled. No
contributor has accepted the Live2D Cubism SDK licence or the Cubism Editor
licence. Two other public implementations, `py-moc3` and `moc3-reader-re`,
derive from a decompilation of Cubism's own exporter and were deliberately not
consulted.

